# What EAS Build uploads. This is a WHITELIST, and deliberately so.
#
# `mobile/` sits inside the website's repo with no npm workspaces joining them, so EAS archives from
# the git root and takes everything. .easignore REPLACES .gitignore rather than adding to it, which
# means every gitignored directory has to be named here or it lands in the archive.
#
# Enumerating what to exclude does not survive contact with a real repo: the first attempt at this
# listed .next/ and missed .next-os/, and the archive went from 664 MB to 2.1 GB — over the limit —
# because a 2.5 GB build cache was silently included. Any new cache directory would do it again.
#
# So: exclude everything at the root, then re-admit only the app.

/*
!/mobile

# ...and within the app, the things that are generated, installed, or secret.
mobile/node_modules/
mobile/.expo/
mobile/dist/
mobile/ios/
mobile/android/

# Development-only credentials — see mobile/lib/devAuth.ts. Gitignored already, but .easignore
# replaces .gitignore for the archive, so leaving this out would upload them to the build server.
mobile/.env*.local
